Intcad is an Intgral fork of SolidCraft. It displays the product name
Intcad and uses Intgral's brand mark. The upstream SolidCraft copyright and
licence notices above remain in force for the upstream code and assets.

Third-party material

Software dependencies are listed in Cargo.lock; their licences are in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt
(`cargo xtask licences`), which the programs also carry (Help > About > Licences,
`intcad-cli licences`). The geometry kernel builds on the truck crates
(truck-modeling, truck-shapeops, truck-meshalgo, truck-stepio, truck-topology and their
dependencies, https://github.com/ricosjp/truck), licensed under the Apache License 2.0 and used
as libraries. truck-shapeops 0.4.0 is vendored in vendor/truck-shapeops with SolidCraft
modifications (listed in vendor/README.md and marked in the source); its licence is in
vendor/truck-shapeops/LICENSE. Copyright (c) RICOS Co. Ltd.

Desktop web view. The Assistant's interface is drawn by the Chromium Embedded Framework
(CEF 154, Chromium 154) that the app is built against. Where a package includes the CEF
runtime, the app loads that distribution as an unmodified library and imports its frames as
GPU textures through the welding and grafting Rust crates (MPL-2.0; grafting is linked as
published, welding is locally modified, and its modified source is in vendor/welding/ of the
matching source revision, recorded in vendor/welding/UPSTREAM.md). CEF and Chromium are BSD
3-Clause; the complete list of third-party components in the Chromium build, with their
licences, is CEF-CREDITS.html, installed with the app's notices. Copyright notices, licence
texts and what each package must ship are in docs/web-view-licences.md,
packaging/notices/WEB-VIEW-PLATFORM-NOTICES.txt and packaging/notices/CEF-CREDITS.html.
There is no system WebView, GTK, WebKitGTK, WebView2 or WKWebView in this build. These are
notices, not a legal clearance.

Vendored graphics HAL. wgpu-hal 30.0.1 is copied into vendor/wgpu-hal from the
locked registry archive (SHA-256 b6b7fb58561a792bc237628ba0792e332de418fefe145f13b5ed8201e6d52f58),
with its original MIT and Apache-2.0 licence texts unchanged and a same-version
Cargo path patch. Its sole local delta is src/vulkan/adapter.rs (early layout
error ownership); vendor/README.md records the change, hashes and removal
criteria. This is modified MIT OR Apache-2.0 source, not a legal clearance.

Modified MPL-2.0 source in vendor/welding/ must be published with the matching
Intcad source revision; the exact covered files and original file hashes are in
vendor/welding/UPSTREAM.md and vendor/README.md. CEF/Chromium runtime provenance,
package signing/notarization, sandbox/helper packaging, the generated credits
version/hash and any bundled LGPL human authorization remain unclosed release
gates, not satisfied by this source tree.


Some code is adapted from sibling projects in the storytold family (CADCraft, GridCraft), which are
licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0; ATTRIBUTION.md lists the files.
The release packaging (.github/workflows/release.yml, packaging/) is adapted from PhotoCraft
(https://github.com/storytold/photocraft), licensed under the Apache License 2.0.

The incremental Radiance RGBE row adapter in crates/render/src/lighting/hdr.rs adapts
decoding state machines from image 0.25.10 (https://github.com/image-rs/image),
MIT OR Apache-2.0. ATTRIBUTION.md describes the bounded/cancellable changes; the
original licence texts are included in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt.

Most bundled assets are drawn in code or contributed originally; third-party fonts (Liberation Sans
for sketch text, BIZ UDPGothic for web Japanese display) are licensed under SIL OFL 1.1. The
per-file list is in ATTRIBUTION.md.

